Problem (Geometry, Level 1):
In the diagram, what is the area of $\triangle ABC$?

[asy]
size(5cm);
real xmax = 15; real ymax = 13; real xmin = -3; real ymin = -3;
pair a = (5, 8); pair b = (0, 0); pair c = (10, 0); draw(b--a--c);
draw((xmin, 0)--(xmax, 0), Arrow); label("$x$", (xmax, 0), E);
draw((0, ymin)--(0, ymax), Arrow); label("$y$", (0, ymax), N);
label("$B(0, 0)$", b, SW);
label("$C(10, 0)$", c, S);
label("$A(5, 8)$", a, N);
[/asy]

Solution:
We think of $BC$ as the base of $\triangle ABC$. Since $B$ is at $(0,0)$ and $C$ is at $(10,0)$, the length of the base is $10 - 0 = 10$.

